title: "When Anti-Sycophancy Training Becomes Stubbornness: A Multilingual Study in English, Russian, and Kazakh"
type: software
version: 1.1.2
date-released: 2026-08-02
authors:
  - family-names: Satybaldy
    given-names: Berik
repository-code: "https://github.com/berikbp/cross-lingual-anti-sycophancy"
url: "https://github.com/berikbp/cross-lingual-anti-sycophancy/releases/tag/v1.1.2"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - sycophancy
  - multilingual evaluation
  - QLoRA
  - language models
abstract: >-
  This artifact studies pressure-induced factual answer changes in English,
  Russian, and Kazakh using matched QLoRA control and intervention adapters.
  A naive intervention produced stubbornness and capability loss. A balanced
  redesign restored capability, but explicit selective feedback did not show
  a reliable pressure-resistance advantage over the matched control. The
  original Kazakh analysis is retained as translation-confounded historical
  evidence. A separately labeled corrected Kazakh sensitivity analysis also
  did not show an intervention advantage.
